# ── video/projects/ — TEXT is shared, MEDIA is local ─────────────────────────
# Founder decision 2026-07-29 (capability video-platform). A video project's TEXT
# is the actual IP and belongs in the repo so teammates can read, review and edit
# each other's films. Its MEDIA is heavy (one 3-minute explainer = 1.8 GB of source
# assets + a 93 MB render) and reproducible, so it stays on the operator's machine.
#
# COMMITTED : SCRIPT.md · FOOTAGE.md · TIMELINE.md/.html · YOUTUBE.md · index.html
#             README.md · run.json   (~130 KB per project)
# LOCAL     : assets/ · build/ · out/
# EXCEPTION : out/filmstrip.jpg — the ONE committed binary. Because media is
#             ignored, this contact sheet is the only auditable evidence that a
#             render was actually verified. ~200 KB, worth its weight.
#
# Consequence /video is built around: a fresh clone has the composition but none
# of the bytes, so `--resume` RE-PROBES the disk and never trusts run.json.
projects/*/assets/
projects/*/build/
projects/*/out/
!projects/*/out/
!projects/*/out/filmstrip.jpg

# ── renders / working artifacts (anywhere under video/) — reproducible ────────
# NB: *.mp4 also blocks committing a reference clip. Intentional — if one must be
# shared, put it in cloud storage and cite the URL in FOOTAGE.md.
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
**/snapshots/
**/.thumbnails/
**/.hyperframes/
**/node_modules/
**/.media/
